    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **51 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` as a derived, read-only response field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nChanges (following the existing derived-field conventions in this codebase):\n\n1. **`TelephoneE164.java`** \u2014 added a `display(String e164)` formatter alongside the existing `normalize`. It splits off the `+` country code (1 digit for `+1`/NANP, 2 otherwise, matching the app's existing country-code handling) and groups the national digits in threes from the left, space-separated. `\"+61412345678\"` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`. Null/non-E.164 input passes through unchanged.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression for `telephoneDisplay` calling `TelephoneE164.display(owner.getTelephone())`, matching how `locality`, `checkDigit`, etc. are derived. This keeps the `model` layer free of any dependency on the `rest` layer.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field into the JSON response.\n\nThe raw `telephone` is unchanged (still normalized to E.164 by `ValidateOwnerFields` and stored verbatim), so both `$.telephone == \"+61412345678\"` and `$.telephoneDisplay == \"+61 412 345 678\"` hold, as `Cp37Tests` asserts.",
